<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαγγᾰν-εύω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάγγανον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>use
			charms</i> or <i>philtres</i>, of Circe, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				310
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>play tricks</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				25.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Gal.</u>
				340a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. πρὸς τὰς θεάς</span>
			<i>use superstitious means</i> to propitiate the goddesses, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				15.29.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐπί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DDeor.</u>
					2.1
				</span></i>
			, <i>Bis Acc.</i><i><span class="en">
				21
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἀπάτην</span>
			<i>contrive means for</i> cheating, <i><span class="en">
				Ach.Tat.
				2.38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>trick out, dress artificially</i>, of cooks, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σιτία καὶ τὰ ὄψα μ. καὶ
					φαρμάττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.126a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
